nds in @gmail.com. A work or school account on Google Workspace uses the organization's own domain, such as jlee@parkviewpm.example. Either way, you use the same Gmail app in a web browser at mail.google.com, so what you practice here works for both."}],["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 mb-4","children":"Key terms"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Google Workspace"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Google's set of work apps (Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Meet, Chat) that an organization manages for its people."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Conversation"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A message and all of its replies, shown together. Gmail groups replies with the original message."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Inbox tabs (categories)"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Primary, Promotions, Social, Updates, and Forums. Gmail sorts incoming mail into the tabs you turn on."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Archive"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Removes a message from the inbox but keeps it. You can still find it in All Mail and by searching."}]]}],"$L20","$L21"]}]]}]]}]]}],"$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25"