23:["$","div","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Inbox tabs sort mail for you"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Gmail can sort incoming mail into tabs across the top of the inbox. Primary holds messages from people you know and anything that doesn't fit another tab. Promotions holds deals and offers. Social holds messages from social networks and media sites. Updates holds confirmations, receipts, bills, and statements. Forums holds messages from online groups and mailing lists. Gmail decides where each message goes, and you can correct it."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"To move a message to the right tab, drag it from the message list onto the tab. A notice appears at the bottom left with Undo in case you dropped it in the wrong place."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"To choose which tabs appear, select Settings (gear) at the top right. In Quick settings, under Inbox type, make sure Default is selected, then select Customize."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Select one or more tabs (categories) and select Save at the bottom of the window. To turn tabs off completely, choose a different inbox type."}]]}],["$","$L2c","2",{"block":{"type":"drag-drop","mode":"sort","title":"Which tab would Gmail use?","prompt":"Drag each message to the inbox tab it most likely lands in.","buckets":[{"id":"primary","label":"Primary"},{"id":"promotions","label":"Promotions"},{"id":"social","label":"Social"},{"id":"updates","label":"Updates"}],"items":[{"id":"a","text":"Denise Carter: “Welcome aboard, Jordan!”","bucket":"primary"},{"id":"b","text":"Office Supply Depot: “30% off printer paper this week”","bucket":"promotions"},{"id":"c","text":"City Water Utility: “Your October statement is ready”","bucket":"updates"},{"id":"d","text":"Neighborly: “3 neighbors posted near Elm Street”","bucket":"social"},{"id":"e","text":"Andre Wallace: “Showing at Elm Street Apartments moved to Thursday”","bucket":"primary"},{"id":"f","text":"An online store: “Your order has shipped”","bucket":"updates"}],"explanation":"Messages from people go to Primary. Deals go to Promotions, social network notices go to Social, and bills, receipts, and shipping notices go to Updates. If Gmail guesses wrong, drag the message to the right tab."}}],["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"If you also use Outlook, the idea is similar to Outlook's Focused and Other tabs: the app sorts mail so the messages from people stand out. In Gmail you can have up to five tabs instead of two."]}]]}]]}]
24:["$","div","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Stars and importance markers"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A star is a flag you set yourself. To star a message, select the star to the left of it in the inbox, or open the message and select the star next to the date. Every starred message appears under Starred in the main menu, and you can search for is:starred."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The importance marker is the tag-shaped marker next to the star. Gmail fills it in yellow when it thinks a message matters, based on things like whom you email often and which messages you open and reply to. Select the marker to correct Gmail; that also teaches it what you consider important. Search for is:important to see every message marked important. If you don't want markers, go to Settings, See all settings, the Inbox tab, and choose No markers under Importance markers."}],["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":""}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Star"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Importance marker"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Who sets it"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"You"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Gmail, and you can correct it"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Use it for"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Messages you need to come back to: a task, a question to answer, a document to read"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"A signal that a sender or topic matters, so Gmail ranks similar mail higher"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Find them"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Starred in the main menu, or search is:starred"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Search is:important (Important under More)"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Star or importance marker?"}]]}]]}]]}]
25:["$","div","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Archive or delete?"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Archiving takes a message out of the inbox without deleting it. It stays in All Mail, it still shows up when you search, and if someone replies, the conversation comes back to your inbox. Use Archive (the box with a down arrow, or the E key) for anything you are done with but might need later: a confirmation, an FYI, a finished conversation."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Deleting moves a message to Trash. You can recover it for up to 30 days: open Trash (under More), check the message, select Move to, and choose where it goes. After 30 days it is permanently deleted. Use Delete for things you will never need, such as an expired sale."}],["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-primary-200 bg-primary-50/50 p-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-700 mb-2","children":"Worked example"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1","children":"Clearing the inbox on your first morning"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Get the Parkview inbox down to the messages that still need you."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":1}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Open the Promotions tab and delete the printer paper sale."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"A sale email has no business value later, so it can go to Trash."}]]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":2}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Archive Kim's FYI about the pest control visit."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"It needs no action, but the office might need to know when the visit happened. Archive keeps it searchable."}]]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Star Denise's welcome message."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"It lists things to ask about this week, so you want to find it quickly under Starred."}]]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":4}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Leave Andre's showing message in the inbox."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"It still needs a reply. The inbox works best as a to-do list of what still needs you."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-primary-200 text-gray-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Result: "}],"The inbox holds only conversations that need action, and nothing useful was thrown away."]}],"$L2d"]}],"$L2e"]}]]}]
26:["$","div","5",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Knowledge Check"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","$L2f","0",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"You archived a message from Kim last week. Where can you find it now?","options":["In Trash","In All Mail, or by searching for it","Nowhere; archiving removes it from Gmail","Only in the Sent folder"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Archiving only removes a message from the inbox. It stays in All Mail and still appears in search results.","optionRationales":["Trash holds deleted messages, not archived ones.","Correct. Archived mail stays in All Mail and shows up in searches.","Archive is the safe choice precisely because it keeps the message.","Sent holds messages you sent. Kim's message was sent to you."]}}],["$","$L2f","1",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"You deleted a vendor's message by mistake three days ago. What should you do?","options":["Nothing; deleted messages are gone immediately","Open Trash, check the message, select Move to, and choose Inbox","Ask the vendor to resend it; Trash can't be opened","Search All Mail; deleted messages stay there"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Deleted messages stay in Trash for up to 30 days, so a message deleted three days ago can still be moved back.","optionRationales":["Messages stay in Trash for up to 30 days before Gmail permanently deletes them.","Correct. Move it out of Trash within 30 days and it's back.","You can open Trash from the main menu (under More) any time.","All Mail doesn't include Trash. Look in Trash itself."]}}],["$","$L2f","2",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Which statement about stars and importance markers is true?","options":["Only Gmail can add stars","You add stars yourself; Gmail sets importance markers and you can correct them","Importance markers delete unimportant mail","Stars and importance markers are the same thing"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Stars are your own flags. Importance markers are Gmail's guesses, and selecting a marker corrects Gmail and helps it learn.","optionRationales":["Stars are yours: select the star next to a message.","Correct.","Markers only flag messages; they never delete anything.","They look different and do different jobs: one is your flag, the other is Gmail's ranking."]}}]]}]]}]
